package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered task-relevant service/configuration and DNS behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["Lifecycle failed-service collection used systemctl and was unsupported on Alpine, so it did not independently inventory failed OpenRC services.","The retained /etc/resolv.conf.head contents were not displayed after restart; its redundancy is inferred from the simultaneously retained 'nohook resolv.conf' configuration and manually managed /etc/resolv.conf."]}
